The microcontroller is the central processing unit of the Weather Detection System.
It is responsible for receiving data from the sensors, processing the signals, 
and converting them into meaningful weather information that can be displayed and stored.
In this project, the microcontroller acts as the main controller that coordinates all system operations.
It continuously reads input data from the temperature, humidity, and rainfall sensors.
After collecting the raw data, it processes and converts it into readable values using programmed instructions.
The microcontroller also manages communication between different components of the system.
It sends processed data to the LCD display for real-time visualization and to the storage module for data logging.
This ensures that users can both view current weather conditions and access historical data when needed.
Additionally, the microcontroller is programmed to operate in a loop, allowing continuous monitoring of environmental conditions. 
It ensures low power consumption and efficient data handling, making the system suitable for long-term use in remote areas.
Overall, the microcontroller plays a crucial role in ensuring the accuracy, reliability, and smooth functioning of the entire Weather Detection System.
Without it, the sensor data would remain unprocessed and unusable.
